Differential Revision: [D35587253](https://our.internmc.facebook.com/intern/diff/D35587253)

Introduce a new optional parameter `hideCommand?: [boolean]` to `IExecOptions` interface to enable ability to hide `[command]` definition output from console when executing `ToolRunner`.

See #830 for reference.

```js
export interface IExecOptions {
    /** optional.  suppress command definition from console output.  defaults to false */
    hideCommand?: boolean;
}
```

### Before
```js
const cmd: ToolRunner = tool(executablePath).arg(executableParameters);
const options: IExecOptions = {};
const exitCode: number = await cmd(options);
```
results in console output
```
[command]/path/to/executable --param1 value1 --param2 value2 --param3 value3
Output from command 1
```

### After
```js
const cmd: ToolRunner = tool(executablePath).arg(executableParameters);
const options: IExecOptions = { hideCommand: true };
const exitCode: number = await cmd(options);
```
results in console output
```
Output from command 1
```

Happy to call the parameter whatever you guys like, if we aren't happy with `hideCommand`.

Also, haven't added any tests since it doesn't look you test those things anyway. Please let me know if you still need some.

